---Makes it possible to redact or flag specified personally identifiable information (PII) in your transcript. If you use ContentRedaction, you must also include the sub-parameters: RedactionOutput and RedactionType. You can optionally include PiiEntityTypes to choose which types of PII you want to redact.
---@class aws.transcribe.ContentRedaction
---@field RedactionType aws.transcribe.RedactionType|string Specify the category of information you want to redact; PII (personally identifiable information) is the only valid value. You can use PiiEntityTypes to choose which types of PII you want to redact. If you do not include PiiEntityTypes in your request, all PII is redacted.
---@field RedactionOutput aws.transcribe.RedactionOutput|string Specify if you want only a redacted transcript, or if you want a redacted and an unredacted transcript.
---@field PiiEntityTypes? aws.transcribe.PiiEntityTypes Specify which types of personally identifiable information (PII) you want to redact in your transcript. You can include as many types as you'd like, or you can select ALL. If you do not include PiiEntityTypes in your request, all PII is redacted.

---@class aws.transcribe.CreateCallAnalyticsCategoryRequest
---@field CategoryName aws.transcribe.CategoryName A unique name, chosen by you, for your Call Analytics category. It's helpful to use a detailed naming system that will make sense to you in the future. For example, it's better to use sentiment-positive-last30seconds for a category over a generic name like test-category.
---@field Rules aws.transcribe.RuleList Rules define a Call Analytics category. When creating a new category, you must create between 1 and 20 rules for that category. For each rule, you specify a filter you want applied to the attributes of a call. For example, you can choose a sentiment filter that detects if a customer's sentiment was positive during the last 30 seconds of the call.
---@field Tags? aws.transcribe.TagList Adds one or more custom tags, each in the form of a key:value pair, to a new call analytics category at the time you start this new job.
---@field InputType? aws.transcribe.InputType|string Choose whether you want to create a real-time or a post-call category for your Call Analytics transcription.

---@class aws.transcribe.CreateCallAnalyticsCategoryResponse
---@field CategoryProperties? aws.transcribe.CategoryProperties Provides you with the properties of your new category, including its associated rules.

