---Flag the presence or absence of specific words or phrases detected in your Call Analytics transcription output.
---@class aws.transcribe.TranscriptFilter
---@field TranscriptFilterType aws.transcribe.TranscriptFilterType|string Flag the presence or absence of an exact match to the phrases that you specify. For example, if you specify the phrase "speak to a manager" as your Targets value, only that exact phrase is flagged.
---@field AbsoluteTimeRange? aws.transcribe.AbsoluteTimeRange Makes it possible to specify a time range (in milliseconds) in your audio, during which you want to search for the specified key words or phrases. See for more detail.
---@field RelativeTimeRange? aws.transcribe.RelativeTimeRange Makes it possible to specify a time range (in percentage) in your media file, during which you want to search for the specified key words or phrases. See for more detail.
---@field ParticipantRole? aws.transcribe.ParticipantRole|string Specify the participant that you want to flag. Omitting this parameter is equivalent to specifying both participants.
---@field Negate? aws.transcribe.Boolean Set to TRUE to flag the absence of the phrase that you specified in your request. Set to FALSE to flag the presence of the phrase that you specified in your request.
---@field Targets aws.transcribe.StringTargetList Specify the phrases that you want to flag.

---@alias aws.transcribe.TranscriptFilterType "EXACT"

---Provides detailed information about a transcription job.
---@class aws.transcribe.TranscriptionJob
---@field TranscriptionJobName? aws.transcribe.TranscriptionJobName The name of the transcription job. Job names are case sensitive and must be unique within an Amazon Web Services account.
---@field TranscriptionJobStatus? aws.transcribe.TranscriptionJobStatus Provides the status of the specified transcription job.
---@field LanguageCode? aws.transcribe.LanguageCode The language code used to create your transcription job. This parameter is used with single-language identification. For multi-language identification requests, refer to the plural version of this parameter, LanguageCodes.
---@field MediaSampleRateHertz? aws.transcribe.MediaSampleRateHertz The sample rate, in hertz, of the audio track in your input media file.
---@field MediaFormat? aws.transcribe.MediaFormat The format of the input media file.
---@field Media? aws.transcribe.Media Provides the Amazon S3 location of the media file you used in your request.
---@field Transcript? aws.transcribe.Transcript Provides you with the Amazon S3 URI you can use to access your transcript.
---@field StartTime? aws.transcribe.DateTime The date and time the specified transcription job began processing.
---@field CreationTime? aws.transcribe.DateTime The date and time the specified transcription job request was made.
---@field CompletionTime? aws.transcribe.DateTime The date and time the specified transcription job finished processing.
---@field FailureReason? aws.transcribe.FailureReason If TranscriptionJobStatus is FAILED, FailureReason contains information about why the transcription job request failed.
---@field Settings? aws.transcribe.Settings Provides information on any additional settings that were included in your request. Additional settings include channel identification, alternative transcriptions, speaker partitioning, custom vocabularies, and custom vocabulary filters.
---@field ModelSettings? aws.transcribe.ModelSettings Provides information on the custom language model you included in your request.
---@field JobExecutionSettings? aws.transcribe.JobExecutionSettings Provides information about how your transcription job was processed. This parameter shows if your request was queued and what data access role was used.
---@field ContentRedaction? aws.transcribe.ContentRedaction Indicates whether redaction was enabled in your transcript.
---@field IdentifyLanguage? aws.transcribe.Boolean Indicates whether automatic language identification was enabled (TRUE) for the specified transcription job.
---@field IdentifyMultipleLanguages? aws.transcribe.Boolean Indicates whether automatic multi-language identification was enabled (TRUE) for the specified transcription job.
---@field LanguageOptions? aws.transcribe.LanguageOptions Provides the language codes you specified in your request.
---@field IdentifiedLanguageScore? aws.transcribe.IdentifiedLanguageScore The confidence score associated with the language identified in your media file.
---@field LanguageCodes? aws.transcribe.LanguageCodeList The language codes used to create your transcription job. This parameter is used with multi-language identification. For single-language identification requests, refer to the singular version of this parameter, LanguageCode.
---@field Tags? aws.transcribe.TagList The tags, each in the form of a key:value pair, assigned to the specified transcription job.
---@field Subtitles? aws.transcribe.SubtitlesOutput Indicates whether subtitles were generated with your transcription.
---@field LanguageIdSettings? aws.transcribe.LanguageIdSettingsMap Provides the name and language of all custom language models, custom vocabularies, and custom vocabulary filters that you included in your request.
---@field ToxicityDetection? aws.transcribe.ToxicityDetection Provides information about the toxicity detection settings applied to your transcription.

